                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 1908,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1026,
                            "last_played": 1793903636
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Hit or miss old-school JRPG with a very unique, yet troublesome, mechanic of having 3 units per \"commander\" hero. With 20 commanders and only 9 at a time that's able to be deployed, there is about 36-80 of characters with 3 simple abilities to keep track of at the same time. It infuriates some but I find it different enough to be refreshing. I like keeping track of that many units, seeing how each of them work and what counters what. Even if the game gets very grindy as a result, even at the easiest difficulty\n\nMy main issue with most Aldorlea RPGs, as usual, is that there are VERY strong, almost important, goodies that you need to backtrack towards with NO indication nor implication of it existing. Once you're in the area after getting the vampire commander(at this point or sometime after), go back to where you got the Bandit hero. There is an artifact that gives you 6GP per each fight won (per wave). Very important",
